The telemetry points to a single root cause: the search service is down, and its failure reaches users through frontend's `/hotels` endpoint.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_deployment_name AS deployment, count(*) AS n, avg(value) AS avg_available, min(value) AS min_v, max(value) AS max_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name = 'search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search deployment reports available=0 in every abnormal sample (19 of 19), versus 1 in normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' AS p, metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, min(time) AS t0, max(time) AS t1, avg(value) AS v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.ready','k8s.container.restarts','k8s.pod.phase') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "The search pod stays not-ready (ready=0) with restarts and phase changed for the whole abnormal window."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, avg(duration)/1e6 AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Abnormal traces contain no search server spans; frontend's search client calls all error in about 0.02 ms.",
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level = 'ERROR' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend logs 515 'Search service failed' errors during the abnormal window; search emits no logs at all."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name IN ('search.Search/Nearby', 'HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "All 952 frontend calls to search fail with Error, and every frontend HTTP /hotels request returns 500."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

